      ],
      "source": "https://icas-nsn.gov/nuiqsut/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nuiqsut sits on the Colville River, about five miles north of its confluence with the Itkillik River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuiqsut%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Nuiqsut is accessible during winter via an ice road, a vital link for supplies and travel.",
